# prose-audit: Grade A — The opening establishes our returned caucus, internal bargain, opposition role and monthly political rhythm in one voice.
title: Red Autumn
new-page: true

= October 2019 — The Left returns

For four years, we watched the Sejm from outside. Now **49 deputies** return
under one banner—and we bring our old rivalries with us.

SLD gives us the party machine, Wiosna a public profile and Razem a movement
and programme. Trade-unionists, feminists and local organisers complete an
alliance that agreed how to win seats, not what we would do with them.

Morawiecki and PiS still command a majority. Andrzej Duda holds the Palace.
We must turn opposition seats into power without being swallowed by larger
parties—or broken by our own alliance.

Each month, choose one fight. Draw opportunities from party politics,
government relations and foreign affairs; keep up to three and play one. Cards
left on the table remain available, but history keeps moving.

The campaign ends in **December 2026**. Its verdict will measure more than
votes: what the Polish left built, changed and survived.

